press for being the only gold medal – albeit in a demonstration sport – that Canada acquired at the Games, but it did little to soften the blow of the country’s failure, for the second time, to achieve gold in an official event at an Olympics hosted on their home soil. Third place went to Norway’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/900527"} "Trine Trulsen"] ", who had been a consistent competitor on the international scene since the mid-1980s and whose brother " [:a {:href "/athletes/102067"} "Pål"] " and husband " [:a {:href "/athletes/102068"} "Lars Vågberg"] " would win gold medals at the 2002 Winter Olympic curling tournament."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {}] [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Team"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Won"] [:th {} "Tied"] [:th {} "Lost"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {:class "accordion-toggle", :data-toggle "collapse", :data-target ".team-members-9012973"} [:div {:class "glyphicon glyphicon-plus"}]] [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "Canada"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CAN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CAN.png"}] "CAN"]] [:td {} "7"] [:td {} "0"] [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "14"] [:td {} "55-40"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class " accordion-body team-members-9012973 collapse", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {} "Skip"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/900102"} "Linda Moore"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–-–"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class " accordion-body team-members-9012973 collapse", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {} "Lead"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/900105"} "Penny Ryan"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–-–"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class " accordion-body team-members-9012973 collapse", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {} "Second"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/9000